# Vercel Function Storage optimization
# Prevent unnecessary files from being uploaded to Vercel Functions

# Test suites and fixtures
tests/
test-results/
.playwright/

# Git and CI
# NOT ignored on purpose: .git/. vercel.json's ignoreCommand
# (scripts/vercel-ignore-build.sh) runs `git diff` in this checkout to skip builds
# that touch no build input. With .git/ listed here it saw no git checkout and
# built every commit (measured 2026-10-08: "BUILD -- no git checkout here").
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Development and build artifacts
dist/
.vite/
.turbo/
.eslintcache
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local environment and config
.env.local
.env.*.local
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Configuration files not needed in runtime (build-time-required configs --
# vite.config.ts, react-router.config.ts, postcss.config.js,
# tailwind.config.ts, tsconfig.*.json -- must stay OUT of this list:
# `vercel build` runs `react-router build` from source on Vercel's infra, so
# anything the build step itself reads has to survive .vercelignore, not
# just anything needed at request time. tsconfig.*.json specifically: react-
# router.config.ts is parsed via tsconfck, which resolves and parses
# tsconfig.app.json even though nothing in the build calls tsc directly)
vitest.config.ts
playwright.config.ts
eslint.config.js

# Documentation and guides
CLAUDE.md
README.md
docs/
PRODUCT.md
*.md

# Dependency cache (Vercel installs fresh on deploy)
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
.pnpm-store/

# Scripts and tooling (not needed at runtime). Glob-excluded like bin/ below so
# the Ignored Build Step script survives: vercel.json's ignoreCommand runs
# `sh scripts/vercel-ignore-build.sh` in the deployed checkout. If it were
# stripped, sh would exit 127, which Vercel reads as BUILD -- safe, but every
# docs-only commit would build again.
scripts/*
!scripts/vercel-ignore-build.sh
# bin/ is glob-excluded rather than dir-excluded so this one entry can be
# un-ignored -- postinstall (package.json) requires it during `npm install`,
# before build even starts, so it can't just be built/copied in later.
bin/*
!bin/install-hooks.cjs
.claude/
.githooks/

# public/ must NOT be ignored -- the same footgun as the build-time configs
# above. `vercel build` runs `react-router build` from source on Vercel's
# infra, and Vite copies public/ into build/client/ as a BUILD INPUT, not a
# runtime-served directory. Ignoring it uploaded a source tree with no
# public/, so the build emitted no favicon, apple-touch-icon, og-image,
# site.webmanifest or robots.txt, and every one of those paths fell through
# to the SPA catchall as 200 text/html: broken social previews, and a
# robots.txt that silently stopped applying the crawl-volume limits this arc
# added to keep bots off the Vercel meter. Local builds have public/ on
# disk, so it reproduced nowhere but production. Shipping it costs 213 KB.

# Database and migrations (authority in admin repo). Anchored to the repo
# root (/supabase/) -- an unanchored "supabase/" is a gitignore-semantics
# footgun: it matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, so it was also
# stripping src/integrations/supabase/ (10 files) from the uploaded source,
# causing `vercel build` to fail on a random missing module each run
# depending on parallel-transform ordering (whichever file under that
# directory got hit first).
/supabase/

# Temporary and log files
*.log
.npmrc
